@ddd.value-object

Purpose:
  Immutable value without identity.

Owns: references\ddd\value-object.sdd
UseWhen:
  - describes a quantity or measurement
  - equality is based on attributes
  - immutability is desired

AvoidWhen:
  - object has lifecycle
  - identity matters
  - frequent mutations expected

Why:
  Value objects reduce complexity by being immutable and interchangeable.

Related:
  @ddd.entity
  @ddd.aggregate

Examples:
  @project.payment
  @project.order

State: +
